module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.LocalRing
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic

/-!
# Completion of a discrete valuation ring

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Lemma Tag 0AP1, the forward direction, with
Algebra, Lemma Tag 00PD (4) (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-completion-of-dvr-is-dvr).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace AdicCompletion

/-- (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-completion-of-dvr-is-dvr)
The maximal-ideal-adic completion of a discrete valuation ring (a Noetherian local domain
whose maximal ideal has one nonzero generator, Stacks Algebra Tag 00PD (4); Mathlib's
`IsDiscreteValuationRing`) is a domain and again a discrete valuation ring (Stacks Project,
More on Algebra, Tag 0AP1, forward direction).

Proof from the node's six steps:
1. Choose a nonzero generator `π` of the maximal ideal. The completion is Noetherian and
   local, and its maximal ideal is the extension of the original maximal ideal, hence is
   generated by the image of `π` (`lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-noetherian`,
   `lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-local-ring`).
2. Every nonzero element of `A` is a unit times a power of `π`
   (`lem-weil-pbc-dvr-unit-times-uniformizer-power`). Thus every nonzero prime contains `π`
   and equals the maximal ideal. The only primes are zero and the nonzero maximal ideal,
   so `A` has dimension one.
3. The maximal ideal has one generator, so `A` is regular local of dimension one
   (`def-weil-regular-scheme`, Stacks Tag 00KU).
4. Its completion is regular local and has the same dimension, namely one
   (`lem-weil-pbc-completion-regular-local`, `lem-weil-pbc-completion-dimension`).
5. A regular local ring is a domain (`lem-sc-regular-local-domain`, Stacks Tag 00NP).
6. The image of `π` is nonzero: otherwise the maximal ideal of the completion would be zero
   and its dimension would be zero, contrary to step 4. Thus the completion is a Noetherian
   local domain whose maximal ideal has a nonzero generator, a discrete valuation ring by
   Stacks Tag 00PD (4). -/
theorem isDiscreteValuationRing
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A] :
    ∃ _ : IsDomain (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A),
      IsDiscreteValuationRing (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) := by
  sorry

end AdicCompletion
